gtkhash (1.5-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix Deepin File Manager integration for portable AppImage builds:
    - When the integration is enabled while GtkHash runs from an AppImage
      (APPIMAGE environment variable set), the AppImage is copied next to
      the launcher script as "GtkHash-x86_64.AppImage", so the context-menu
      keeps working even if the user later moves or renames the original
      AppImage file.
    - Disabling the integration now also removes that copied AppImage.
    - The launcher script template is now robust: it supports a manually
      configured path, a recorded "appimage-path" file, any file matching
      GtkHash*.AppImage in common locations, and a bounded $HOME search,
      so moving/renaming the AppImage no longer breaks the menu entry.
  * Add missing <gio/gio.h> include used by the new file-copy code.

 -- Deepin Builder <builder@localhost>  Sun, 04 Oct 2026 00:40:29 +0800

